{"type":"text","timestamp":1794582827027,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","part":{"id":"prt_1d578cec6002vB5ekFhTYkAxIi","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","messageID":"msg_1d578871f001eqKg3sT2JhmGoN","type":"text","text":"Now let me enumerate every occurrence of the old-name pattern in the seven files.\n\n","time":{"start":1794582826694,"end":1794582827027}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582827092,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d578cec8002tgWYkDqsY5DvWW","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","messageID":"msg_1d578871f001eqKg3sT2JhmGoN","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-90c790f05a1c8fb1","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -P \"/create:skill(?![-\\w])|(?<![-\\w/])create:skill(?![-\\w])|create/skill\\.md|command-create-skill(?![-\\w])\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/README.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/command-metadata-schema.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:811:  assert.deepEqual(schemaCodes([validEntry({ command: 'create:skill' })]), ['BAD_COMMAND_ID']);\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:838:  assert.equal(commandSchema.commandDefinitionRelPath('/create:skill'), 'create/skill.md');\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:17:The shared field vocabulary that `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/doctor:skill-advisor tune`, and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` all render after touching a skill root, so that scaffolding a skill and diagnosing its advisor state describe the same reality in the same words.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:104:H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (class-S) roots — `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` are structurally forbidden there (`skill-root-metadata-contract.md` §3). `command-metadata.json` is optional on both classes, so a standalone result reports it only when the root ships it. A standalone `/create:skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong; it should not mention the field at all.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:106:**Guardrail (do not build this):** `description.json` stays descriptive and is never validated against graph vocabulary, and standalone `/create:skill` never asserts parent-hub metadata files. This boundary was raised and re-confirmed across nine iterations of research (Theme C, research.md) specifically because it is the mistake future maintainers are most likely to reintroduce — resist adding a `description.json` ↔ `graph-metadata.json` equality check or a parent-file requirement to a standalone assertion, however tempting it looks as a \"consistency\" improvement.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:114:| Standalone `/create:skill` full-create | Full handoff, `standalone` scope (H-only fields omitted) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:115:| Standalone `/create:skill` full-update | Full handoff, `standalone` scope |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:37:- You are creating a brand-new skill from scratch. Use `/create:skill` or `/create:skill-parent` directly. See [creation-workflow.md](creation-workflow.md) and [parent-skills-nested-packets.md](../parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md)\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:43:- `/create:skill` - standalone scaffold and repair (`full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, `asset-only`)\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:207:A standalone root keeps `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json`, and `leaf-manifest.config.json`. Its `SKILL.md` links to `./ROUTER.md`. It must not gain `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json` or `description.json`. It may add `command-metadata.json` when it owns slash commands, with each entry's `ownerMode` set to the skill's own id. Repair that package with `/create:skill <skill-name> full-update` (or `reference-only` / `asset-only` for a scoped add). `/create:skill <skill-name> full-create` is only for a folder that does not exist yet.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md:270:- `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` - `/create:skill` operations `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, `asset-only`\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md:20:- Running `/create:skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md:26:Keyword triggers: `create skill`, `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `package skill`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/command-metadata-schema.cjs:201: * `/create:skill` → `create/skill.md` and `/prompt:improve` → `prompt/improve.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:27:Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:33:- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the nine `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:97:    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/README.md:23:| **Invoke with** | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, \"new skill\", \"parent hub\" |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:811:  assert.deepEqual(schemaCodes([validEntry({ command: 'create:skill' })]), ['BAD_COMMAND_ID']);\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:838:  assert.equal(commandSchema.commandDefinitionRelPath('/create:skill'), 'create/skill.md');\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:17:The shared field vocabulary that `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/doctor:skill-advisor tune`, and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` all render after touching a skill root, so that scaffolding a skill and diagnosing its advisor state describe the same reality in the same words.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:104:H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (class-S) roots — `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` are structurally forbidden there (`skill-root-metadata-contract.md` §3). `command-metadata.json` is optional on both classes, so a standalone result reports it only when the root ships it. A standalone `/create:skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong; it should not mention the field at all.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md:106:**Guardrail (do not build this):** `description.json` stays descriptive and is never