a skill and diagnosing its advisor state describe the same reality in the same words.\n \n ---\n \n ## 1. OVERVIEW\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"The shared field vocabulary that `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/doctor:skill-advisor tune`, and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` all render\", \"oldString\": \"The shared field vocabulary that `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/doctor:skill-advisor tune`, and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` all render\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582872758,"end":1794582876771}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582876775,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d57961a3001vgCu4Er14PT1DG","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","messageID":"msg_1d5794df1001RZNCRA071q4ZQi","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-85faefdc8da03b16","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Running `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.","oldString":"- Running `/create:skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\n@@ -16,9 +16,9 @@\n ### Activation Triggers\n \n Use this packet when the request involves:\n - Creating or rebuilding an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`.\n-- Running `/create:skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.\n+- Running `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.\n - Running `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub with nested workflow or surface packets.\n - Authoring or repairing `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/`, or `changelog/` for a skill package.\n - Creating parent-hub router files such as `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json`, `description.json`, or hub-level `graph-metadata.json`.\n - Validating and packaging a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Running `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.\", \"oldString\": \"- Running `/create:skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582864291,"end":1794582876775}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582876782,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5798315001v3p3OoO3tlgk6F","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827cfffePFfrjkEfSEl2K2","messageID":"msg_1d5794df1001RZNCRA071q4ZQi","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ca62b65e615ecf7","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"A standalone `/create:sk-skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong","oldString":"A standalone `/create:skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\n@@ -100,9 +100,9 @@\n ---\n \n ## 5. CLASS APPLICABILITY\n \n-H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (class-S) roots — `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` are structurally forbidden there (`skill-root-metadata-contract.md` §3). `command-metadata.json` is optional on both classes, so a standalone result reports it only when the root ships it. A standalone `/create:skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong; it should not mention the field at all.\n+H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (class-S) roots — `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` are structurally forbidden there (`skill-root-metadata-contract.md` §3). `command-metadata.json` is optional on both classes, so a standalone result reports it only when the root ships it. A standalone `/create:sk-skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong; it should not mention the field at all.\n \n **Guardrail (do not build this):** `description.json` stays descriptive and is never validated against graph vocabulary, and standalone `/create:skill` never asserts parent-hub metadata files. This boundary was raised and re-confirmed across nine iterations of research (Theme C, research.md) specifically because it is the mistake future maintainers are most likely to reintroduce — resist adding a `description.json` ↔ `graph-metadata.json` equality check or a parent-file requirement to a standalone assertion, however tempting it looks as a \"consistency\" improvement.\n \n ---\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"A standalone `/create:sk-skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong\", \"oldString\": \"A standalone `/create:skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582872853,"end":1794582876782}}}}
