des load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n+Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n@@ -33 +33 @@ Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill\n-- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the nine `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`.\n+- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the nine `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`.\n@@ -97 +97 @@ INTENT_MODEL = {\n-    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n+    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:sk-skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\nindex 5527105d35..4052797b6c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\n@@ -20 +20 @@ Use this packet when the request involves:\n-- Running `/create:skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.\n+- Running `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill with its own advisor identity.\n@@ -26 +26 @@ Use this packet when the request involves:\n-Keyword triggers: `create skill`, `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `package skill`.\n+Keyword triggers: `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `package skill`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\nindex 4ca9fa7a14..3ac2ebfa76 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\n@@ -17 +17 @@ version: 1.2.3.0\n-The shared field vocabulary that `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/doctor:skill-advisor tune`, and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` all render after touching a skill root, so that scaffolding a skill and diagnosing its advisor state describe the same reality in the same words.\n+The shared field vocabulary that `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/doctor:skill-advisor tune`, and `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` all render after touching a skill root, so that scaffolding a skill and diagnosing its advisor state describe the same reality in the same words.\n@@ -104 +104 @@ Doctor severity derivation for `skill_graph_validate` (`pass`/`warn`/`fail`/`una\n-H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (class-S) roots — `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` are structurally forbidden there (`skill-root-metadata-contract.md` §3). `command-metadata.json` is optional on both classes, so a standalone result reports it only when the root ships it. A standalone `/create:skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong; it should not mention the field at all.\n+H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (class-S) roots — `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` are structurally forbidden there (`skill-root-metadata-contract.md` §3). `command-metadata.json` is optional on both classes, so a standalone result reports it only when the root ships it. A standalone `/create:sk-skill` result that reported `description.json: MISSING` would be wrong; it should not mention the field at all.\n@@ -106 +106 @@ H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (\n-**Guardrail (do not build this):** `description.json` stays descriptive and is never validated against graph vocabulary, and standalone `/create:skill` never asserts parent-hub metadata files. This boundary was raised and re-confirmed across nine iterations of research (Theme C, research.md) specifically because it is the mistake future maintainers are most likely to reintroduce — resist adding a `description.json` ↔ `graph-metadata.json` equality check or a parent-file requirement to a standalone assertion, however tempting it looks as a \"consistency\" improvement.\n+**Guardrail (do not build this):** `description.json` stays descriptive and is never validated against graph vocabulary, and standalone `/create:sk-skill` never asserts parent-hub metadata files. This boundary was raised and re-confirmed across nine iterations of research (Theme C, research.md) specifically because it is the mistake future maintainers are most likely to reintroduce — resist adding a `description.json` ↔ `graph-metadata.json` equality check or a parent-file requirement to a standalone assertion, however tempting it looks as a \"consistency\" improvement.\n@@ -114,2 +114,2 @@ H-only fields render **omitted**, not `N/A` or a false negative, on standalone (\n-| Standalone `/create:skill` full-create | Full handoff, `standalone` scope (H-only fields omitted) |\n-| Standalone `/create:skill` full-update | Full handoff, `standalone` scope |\n+| Standalone `/create:sk-skill` full-create | Full handoff, `standalone` scope (H-only fields omitted) |\n+| Standalone `/create:sk-skill` full-update | Full handoff, `standalone` scope |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\nindex fd20881ea9..4f306b08c9 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\n@@ -37 +37 @@ v4 reshaped `sk-code` into a parent hub: one advisor identity that dispatches to\n-- You are creating a brand-new skill from scratch. Use `/create:skill` or `/create:skill-parent` directly. See [creation-workflow.md](creation-workflow.md) and [parent-skills-nested-packets.md](../parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md)\n+- You are creating a brand-new skill from scratch. Use `/create:sk-skill` or `/create:skill-parent` directly. See [creation-workflow.md](creation-workflow.md) and [parent-skills-nested-packets.md](../parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md)\n@@ -43 +43 @@ v4 reshaped `sk-code` into a parent hub: one advisor identity that dispatches to\n-- `/create:skill` - standalone scaffold and repair (`full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, `asset-only`)\n+- `/create:sk-skill` - standalone scaffold and repair (`full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, `asset-only`)\n@@ -207 +207 @@ Stay on class S when the skill still has one job.\n-A standalone root keeps `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json`, and `leaf-manifest.config.json`. Its `SKILL.md` links to `./ROUTER.md`. It must not gain `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json` or `description.json`. It may add `command-metadata.json` when it owns slash commands, with each entry's `ownerMode` set to the skill's own id. Repair that package with `/create:skill <skill-name> full-update` (or `reference-only` / `asset-only` for a scoped add). `/create:skill <skill-name> full-create` is only for a folder that does not exist yet.\n+A standalone root keeps `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json`, and `leaf-manifest.config.json`. Its `SKILL.md` links to `./ROUTER.md`. It must not gain `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json` or `description.json`. It may add `command-metadata.json` when it owns slash commands, with each entry's `ownerMode` set to the sk